From d52666942d2d4307553eb03ecb9cbda5481ffb79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <tetcu@fgorg.vn>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:32:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(language): add a language-pack extension point

Language packs are separately installed ES modules named by OHS_LANGUAGE_PACK
(options in OHS_LANGUAGE_PACK_OPTIONS). A pack declares up to three lexical
views of every note; each view is indexed in its own FTS5 table and searched
as one extra RRF branch. Packs can rewrite the BM25 and embedding queries, add
exact-alias keys, and rescore fused candidates. Snippets stay original text:
view matches are mapped back through a token-alignment invariant and exposed
as matchedTerms. A new explain option reports per-branch ranks.

Without a pack no view tables exist and results are byte-identical to
upstream. A broken pack is reported in status and ignored. Changing packs
rebuilds only the view tables from stored notes, without re-embedding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
